# Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind

## App Router

- Use the App Router patterns already in the repo (`app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`).
- Add `'use client'` only when the component needs client-only APIs (hooks, browser APIs, event handlers that require client boundaries). Default to server components when possible.

## TypeScript

- `strict` is enabled: prefer explicit prop types (interfaces/types or inline `{ prop: Type }`). Avoid `any`; use `unknown` and narrow when needed.
- Use `import type { ... }` for type-only imports where it improves clarity and matches nearby files.

## React

- Prefer small, composable presentational components under `app/ui/`.
- Keep default-export component style consistent with siblings in the same folder.

## Tailwind CSS

- Utility-first classes; follow spacing, typography, and color patterns from neighboring components.
- Prefer semantic structure (landmarks, headings) where it fits the resume layout.

## Imports

- Use the `@/` alias (e.g. `@/app/ui/...`, `@/app/services/...`).
